But we try so hard to get it right that we sometimes get it wrong.

196
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:45,500
Jesus addressed this with the Pharisees.

197
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:47,260
He called them whitewashed tombs.

198
00:18:47,260 --> 00:18:48,740
He said, you look great on the outside.

199
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:49,940
It looks like you get it.

200
00:18:50,180 --> 00:18:55,560
Everyone around you thinks you're awesome at this religion thing, thinks you're awesome at this Jesus thing, but I know your heart.

201
00:18:55,560 --> 00:18:57,740
I know what's actually going on.

202
00:18:57,740 --> 00:19:03,120
You might be good at pretending like you're good at this thing, but in reality, you're treating people poorly.

203
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:05,280
You're not taking care of the least of these.

204
00:19:05,280 --> 00:19:10,780
If we were to follow this Francis Chan illustration along throughout our talk today,

205
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:18,140
this would be the daughter that runs to the room and grabs all of the mess in her room and shoves it under the bed and sticks it in the closet.

206
00:19:18,140 --> 00:19:19,360
Done.

207
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:22,340
I did the thing that dad told me to do.

208
00:19:22,340 --> 00:19:24,960
But dads are smart, right?

209
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:28,220
You guys know to check under the bed and to look in the closet.

210
00:19:28,220 --> 00:19:29,480
And the same thing is true of God.

211
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:30,740
God knows our hearts.

212
00:19:31,740 --> 00:19:39,560
And so we, out of this desire to be obedient, and also sometimes this desire to be obedient on our own terms,

213
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:47,580
define truth, define religion in a way that we can easily accomplish it.

214
00:19:48,540 --> 00:19:51,680
It's easy to stick everything under the bed and into the closet.

215
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:53,060
It's easy to do that.

216
00:19:53,060 --> 00:19:57,160
And so oftentimes we're like, we want to obey God, but also obeying God is hard.

217
00:19:57,160 --> 00:20:01,160
And so we redefine obedience to God in this, like, I'll just do it really quick.

218
00:20:01,160 --> 00:20:02,240
I'll stick all these things here.

219
00:20:02,240 --> 00:20:03,740
Everybody will think that I'm good at it.

220
00:20:03,740 --> 00:20:05,620
But God knows your heart.

221
00:20:05,620 --> 00:20:09,120
And what happens here is, if we've got a church full of people that are doing that,

222
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:13,260
we look good at being spiritually mature on the outside,

223
00:20:13,260 --> 00:20:14,460
here's what's going to happen.

224
00:20:14,460 --> 00:20:17,460
I'm going to do something that makes you mad.

225
00:20:17,540 --> 00:20:18,980
I'm going to step on your toes.

226
00:20:18,980 --> 00:20:20,480
You're going to step on my toes.

227
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:26,400
And because we're not actually like Jesus, when conflict happens, we'll show our true colors.

228
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:30,060
And a church like that is never going to be unified.

229
00:20:30,060 --> 00:20:34,680
Because a church like that's never going to act like Jesus when things get tough.

230
00:20:34,680 --> 00:20:38,700
Religious people are really good at acting like Jesus when things are great.

231
00:20:38,700 --> 00:20:42,620
When things get tough, what's true in our hearts comes out.

232
00:20:42,620 --> 00:20:44,520
Do we see how this sounds like truth?

233
00:20:44,520 --> 00:20:46,640
But it's a distortion of truth.

234
00:20:46,640 --> 00:20:49,780
Because oftentimes people, out of a good heart, want to obey God.

235
00:20:49,780 --> 00:20:52,100
But they take the shortcut.

236
00:20:52,100 --> 00:20:54,260
This is actually what happened to the church at Ephesus.

237
00:20:56,360 --> 00:21:01,360
Paul writes this beautiful vision casting for a unified church, what a unified church looks like.

238
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:05,880
And he warns them, if you're going to be unified, if you're going to be like Jesus, you can't buy into false teaching.

239
00:21:06,680 --> 00:21:08,780
And so they focus all of their attention.

240
00:21:08,780 --> 00:21:13,900
They set all of their minds and their hearts and their energy to not buying into false teaching.

241
00:21:13,900 --> 00:21:16,200
And this is what happened.

242
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:19,720
John writes this to the church at Ephesus in Revelation chapter 2.

243
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:22,080
This is actually Jesus to the church.

244
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:23,120
He says,

245
00:21:23,120 --> 00:21:24,160
I know all the things you do.

246
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:27,580
I've seen your hard work and your patient endurance.

247
00:21:27,580 --> 00:21:30,760
I know that you cannot tolerate evil.

248
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:34,500
You have examined the claims of those who say they are apostles but are not.

249
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:37,400
You have discovered that they are liars.

250
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:40,740
You have patiently suffered for me without quitting.

251
00:21:42,180 --> 00:21:43,720
This is a pretty good thing, right?

252
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:47,700
We see how the church, they heard Paul's warning and they nailed it.

253
00:21:47,700 --> 00:21:50,940
They now, they can point out false teachers from a mile away.

254
00:21:50,940 --> 00:21:52,840
But what happened in this?

255
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:53,180
He says,

256
00:21:53,180 --> 00:21:55,360
But I have this complaint against you.

257
00:21:55,360 --> 00:21:59,760
You don't love me or each other as you did at first.

258
00:21:59,760 --> 00:22:02,640
Look how far you have fallen.

259
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:05,020
Turn back to me and do the works you did at first.

260
00:22:05,020 --> 00:22:11,500
If you don't repent, I will come and I will remove your lampstand from its place among the churches.

261
00:22:12,180 --> 00:22:18,740
See how they bought this subtle lie of truth without love?

262
00:22:18,740 --> 00:22:25,100
They were so good at pointing out false doctrine that they forgot to love God and love one another.

263
00:22:25,100 --> 00:22:32,020
Out of their desire to be able to point out false teachers, they became themselves false teachers.

264
00:22:32,020 --> 00:22:36,260
They started to teach this lesson that it's all about truth.

265
00:22:36,260 --> 00:22:38,960
And they got it wrong.

266
00:22:38,960 --> 00:22:40,180
And Jesus comes to them and says,

267
00:22:40,180 --> 00:22:41,400
You're missing the mark.

268
00:22:41,420 --> 00:22:47,760
And if you don't fix it, I'm going to take the opportunity for you to be a visible expression of the church to your city away from you.

269
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:48,720
I'll give it to somebody else.

270
00:22:48,720 --> 00:22:50,700
Jesus is going to build His church.

271
00:22:50,700 --> 00:22:52,700
And the gates of hell will not prevail against it.

272
00:22:52,700 --> 00:22:54,480
He doesn't have to use you and me.

273
00:22:54,480 --> 00:22:56,600
We get to be a part of it.

274
00:22:56,600 --> 00:23:01,360
But we've got to get this balance of truth and love right.

275
00:23:01,360 --> 00:23:05,660
Truth without love is a false teaching that leads to spiritual immaturity.

276
00:23:05,760 --> 00:23:09,220
It's a bunch of people that look mature that actually aren't.

277
00:23:09,220 --> 00:23:11,980
Kent quoted this passage last week, 1 Corinthians 13.

278
00:23:11,980 --> 00:23:18,100
If we possess all knowledge, if we have all the information in the world, but we don't love one another.

279
00:23:18,100 --> 00:23:19,300
We don't love God.

280
00:23:19,300 --> 00:23:20,300
We don't love one another.

281
00:23:20,300 --> 00:23:21,580
We're missing the point.

282
00:23:21,580 --> 00:23:27,520
Spiritual maturity isn't measured by how good you are at pointing out how wrong other people are.

283
00:23:28,980 --> 00:23:29,780
He's not.

284
00:23:29,780 --> 00:23:38,060
But, for those of you that are academics, you care about theology, I know that this has been a hard rant.

285
00:23:38,060 --> 00:23:41,180
But I told you a couple weeks ago, I'm an equal opportunity offender.

286
00:23:41,180 --> 00:23:47,440
So, let's transition to the other type of false teaching that tends to creep into the church and get us off track.

287
00:23:47,440 --> 00:23:51,140
It sounds like truth, but it's a distortion.

288
00:23:51,140 --> 00:23:56,140
If spiritual maturity isn't measured by how good you are at pointing out how other people are wrong,

289
00:23:56,140 --> 00:24:00,660
it also doesn't mean that you get to redefine truth to make everyone feel better.

290
00:24:00,660 --> 00:24:02,760
The second, false teaching.

291
00:24:02,760 --> 00:24:06,060
I'm using common language, but it happens all throughout the church.

292
00:24:06,060 --> 00:24:06,960
It will continue to happen.

293
00:24:06,960 --> 00:24:11,320
I'm calling it postmodernism for now, but it's love without truth.

294
00:24:11,320 --> 00:24:17,980
False teachers, they come from outside of the church, and slowly over time it drips in.

295
00:24:17,980 --> 00:24:21,800
Because individual believers, we're not setting our eyes on Jesus.

296
00:24:21,800 --> 00:24:26,420
Rather, we're setting our eyes on teachers that make us feel good, that tell us the things that we want to hear.

297
00:24:26,420 --> 00:24:32,420
And so, instead of becoming more like Jesus, we buy into this teaching that Jesus is all about love without truth.

298
00:24:32,420 --> 00:24:38,520
We've heard this phrase slip into the church, live your truth.

299
00:24:38,520 --> 00:24:41,460
It's a false teaching.

300
00:24:41,460 --> 00:24:43,300
It goes kind of like this.

301
00:24:43,360 --> 00:24:50,240
God loves you, and he wants you to be happy, and the only way that you will be happy is if you live your truth.

302
00:24:50,240 --> 00:24:53,140
Do we hear a subtle lie in there?

303
00:24:53,140 --> 00:24:55,480
God loves you.

304
00:24:55,480 --> 00:24:56,720
Is that true?

305
00:24:56,720 --> 00:24:57,880
True.

306
00:24:57,880 --> 00:24:59,360
God wants you to be happy.

307
00:24:59,360 --> 00:25:03,780
This is an abundant life that God has created for all of his followers of Jesus.

308
00:25:03,780 --> 00:25:07,260
Happiness is kind of a misstep that we've taken there.

309
00:25:07,320 --> 00:25:09,180
But does God want you to have an abundant life?

310
00:25:09,180 --> 00:25:10,120
Yes.

311
00:25:10,120 --> 00:25:14,720
The only way that you will have that abundant life is if you live your truth.

312
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:16,600
No, right?

313
00:25:16,600 --> 00:25:18,760
That's the subtle lie.

314
00:25:18,760 --> 00:25:21,980
It's the same lie that the enemy used in the garden with Adam and Eve.

315
00:25:21,980 --> 00:25:23,120
Did God really say?

316
00:25:23,120 --> 00:25:27,520
Did he really say you couldn't eat of this tree?

317
00:25:27,520 --> 00:25:34,140
We begin to redefine truth based on our own desires and the desires of others.

318
00:25:35,040 --> 00:25:40,520
If we go back to the Francis Chan illustration, the dad comes in.

319
00:25:40,520 --> 00:25:41,340
The room's a mess.

320
00:25:41,340 --> 00:25:43,820
Daughter's sitting there, and he says, what's going on?

321
00:25:43,820 --> 00:25:44,940
Your room's a mess.

322
00:25:44,940 --> 00:25:48,600
She says, what really is clean anyway?

323
00:25:48,600 --> 00:25:53,020
Who gets to define what clean means?

324
00:25:53,020 --> 00:25:55,800
Who made you the authority of what clean means?

325
00:25:55,800 --> 00:25:57,180
This room feels clean to me.

326
00:25:57,180 --> 00:25:57,960
It looks clean to me.

327
00:25:57,960 --> 00:25:59,960
I think this room is clean.

328
00:26:01,500 --> 00:26:09,040
And, again, I'm being hard on both groups of people because I've found myself in both categories all of the time.

329
00:26:09,040 --> 00:26:10,880
And oftentimes, I know my heart.

330
00:26:10,880 --> 00:26:13,860
Sometimes it's out of a really bad, evil temptation.

331
00:26:13,860 --> 00:26:17,920
But oftentimes, I really just want people to experience the love of God.

332
00:26:17,920 --> 00:26:25,620
God loves me so much that he sent his son, his one and only son, to die in your place for your sins.

333
00:26:25,620 --> 00:26:30,180
I want people who are outside of that to understand how deep the love of the Father is.

334
00:26:30,180 --> 00:26:35,900
But oftentimes, because I'm afraid of the whole truth thing and how they're going to take it, I'll water it down.

335
00:26:37,120 --> 00:26:41,320
This is where the Jewish people found themselves when Jesus came.

336
00:26:41,320 --> 00:26:45,980
And you see the crowds kind of like all coming to Jesus.

337
00:26:45,980 --> 00:26:49,420
And I think the reason the crowd came to Jesus is there was a vacuum in leadership.

338
00:26:49,420 --> 00:26:52,040
They were being pulled by Rome in one way.

339
00:26:52,040 --> 00:26:54,840
They were being pulled by the Jewish kings in another way.

340
00:26:54,840 --> 00:26:58,400
And they had no clue what real truth actually looked like.

341
00:26:58,460 --> 00:27:00,320
And Jesus looked at them with compassion.

342
00:27:00,320 --> 00:27:03,020
And he said, they're like sheep without a shepherd.

343
00:27:03,020 --> 00:27:11,280
And that's how Jesus looks at people that are buying into this false teaching that love without truth.

344
00:27:11,280 --> 00:27:14,900
He looks at us and says, they're like a sheep without a shepherd.

345
00:27:14,900 --> 00:27:15,760
Let me lead you.

346
00:27:15,760 --> 00:27:16,480
Let me guide you.

347
00:27:16,480 --> 00:27:19,860
Let me direct you in the way that things should go.

348
00:27:22,040 --> 00:27:31,500
So what happens to a church that's filled with religious people is we step on each other's toes, we get mad, conflict happens because we're not actually spiritually mature.

349
00:27:31,500 --> 00:27:35,480
What happens to a church of people that are building their life on this false teaching?

350
00:27:35,480 --> 00:27:41,400
I think we actually have a picture of the worst-case scenario in 1 Corinthians.

351
00:27:41,400 --> 00:27:45,460
A church that focuses all about love without truth.

352
00:27:45,460 --> 00:27:50,320
Eventually, somebody comes to the communion table bragging about how they're sleeping with their mother.

353
00:27:52,040 --> 00:28:01,020
When truth gets so watered down and the love of God is so pushed to this idea, what happens is we start to brag about our sin.

354
00:28:01,020 --> 00:28:04,780
We start to celebrate the stuff that God doesn't love in us.

355
00:28:04,780 --> 00:28:06,600
He's trying to round that stuff out.

356
00:28:06,600 --> 00:28:09,060
He's trying to call us to obedience to Jesus.

357
00:28:09,060 --> 00:28:13,220
And instead, we're so focused on the love thing that we start to brag about sin.

358
00:28:13,220 --> 00:28:21,200
Spiritual maturity is defined by obedience to Jesus, not the ability to redefine truth in a way that fits your agenda.

359
00:28:22,040 --> 00:28:22,880
Love with no truth.

360
00:28:22,880 --> 00:28:32,420
Love with no truth might produce a shallow harmony, but it will never produce this real, genuine unity that Paul has in mind for the church.

361
00:28:33,500 --> 00:28:42,580
See, Jesus, Jesus is the perfect balance of truth and love.

362
00:28:42,580 --> 00:28:53,520
And if we're going to get this right, if we're going to be individuals that are spiritually mature, we have to set our eyes on Jesus and we have to become a people that, as Paul says in verse 15,

363
00:28:55,020 --> 00:29:02,960
speak the truth and love, growing in every way more and more like Christ who is the head of the body, the church.

364
00:29:02,960 --> 00:29:09,100
If we're going to get this right, if we're going to be a unified church, we've got to get spiritual maturity right.

365
00:29:09,100 --> 00:29:15,140
If we're going to get spiritual maturity right, we have to get this balance of truth and love right.

366
00:29:15,140 --> 00:29:22,700
And those of us, those of us that have been following Jesus for any time at all, this is the most attractive thing about Jesus.

367
00:29:22,700 --> 00:29:27,580
This is abundant life.

368
00:29:27,580 --> 00:29:35,800
Like coming to the author and creator of all things and having him call us out on the things that aren't going to lead us to life,

369
00:29:35,800 --> 00:29:41,540
but doing it in such a way that is so loving and so gracious like a shepherd leading his sheep down the right path.

370
00:29:42,660 --> 00:29:44,700
This is what we long for.

371
00:29:44,700 --> 00:29:51,280
But we mess this balance up all the time.

372
00:29:51,280 --> 00:29:56,100
Love what Hebrews chapter 12 says.

373
00:29:56,100 --> 00:30:02,200
It says, let us strip off every weight that slows us down, especially the sin that so easily trips us up,

374
00:30:02,200 --> 00:30:06,460
and let us run with endurance the race that God has set before us.

375
00:30:06,460 --> 00:30:11,800
We do this by keeping our eyes on Jesus, the perfect balance of truth and love.

376
00:30:11,860 --> 00:30:19,140
And as each one of us as individuals set our eyes on Jesus, the champion who initiates and perfects our faith,

377
00:30:19,140 --> 00:30:20,620
he is the author of it all.

378
00:30:20,620 --> 00:30:24,620
It all happened because of the joy awaiting him.

379
00:30:24,620 --> 00:30:29,360
He endured the cross disregarding its name and now is seated at the place of honor.

380
00:30:29,360 --> 00:30:35,020
The cross is the perfect balance of truth and love.

381
00:30:36,380 --> 00:30:37,720
So what's the result?

382
00:30:37,720 --> 00:30:39,540
What happens if we do this?

383
00:30:39,540 --> 00:30:47,180
Well, verse 16, if every individual in this church takes seriously the command to look at Jesus,

384
00:30:47,180 --> 00:30:51,520
to set your eyes on Jesus, to understand this balance of truth and love,

385
00:30:51,520 --> 00:30:55,140
to not buy into false teaching, but to set your eyes on Jesus,

386
00:30:55,140 --> 00:31:00,900
he, Jesus, makes the whole body fit together perfectly.

387
00:31:01,440 --> 00:31:10,860
As each part does its own special work, it helps the other parts grow so that the whole body is healthy and growing and full of love.

388
00:31:14,200 --> 00:31:17,880
Individual maturity will lead to church unity.

389
00:31:17,880 --> 00:31:25,360
If we become more like Jesus, as individuals, we will become more like Jesus as a church.

390
00:31:27,440 --> 00:31:31,940
This is what Jesus meant when he talked to his disciples right before he went to the cross.

391
00:31:31,940 --> 00:31:36,320
And he said, the world will know that you are my disciples by the way that you love one another.

392
00:31:36,320 --> 00:31:38,940
We've got to get this right.

393
00:31:38,940 --> 00:31:43,480
And as we get this right, people from the outside will say, whoa, you guys have something.

394
00:31:43,480 --> 00:31:46,640
It's not truth without love.

395
00:31:46,640 --> 00:31:50,380
It's not fake throwing dirty clothes under the bed and in the closet.

396
00:31:50,380 --> 00:31:52,080
Like, you guys are real authentic.

397
00:31:52,280 --> 00:31:57,340
You're honest about the ways you struggle, but you're setting your eyes on Jesus, the author, perfecter of your faith.

398
00:31:57,340 --> 00:32:02,760
And it's also not this, like, everybody can do whatever they want kind of thing.

399
00:32:02,760 --> 00:32:04,700
Like, there's accountability.

400
00:32:04,700 --> 00:32:07,040
There's truth.

401
00:32:07,040 --> 00:32:09,860
This is what the world needs from us.

402
00:32:09,860 --> 00:32:15,180
It needs individual believers setting their eyes on Jesus, understanding the perfect balance of truth and love.

403
00:32:15,180 --> 00:32:19,800
And as we grow in this, church unity will be the result.

404
00:32:21,200 --> 00:32:25,820
A couple of weeks ago, I gave my first message, and Barrett came up to me afterwards.

405
00:32:25,820 --> 00:32:32,300
And she said that Dave Winsett, when Barrett and Jason were getting married, drew this little picture here of this triangle.

406
00:32:32,300 --> 00:32:38,480
And this triangle kind of has the two, the husband and wife, at the bottom of the triangle.

407
00:32:38,480 --> 00:32:46,120
And Dave said, if you want to be a unified couple, what we tend to think needs to happen is we need to look to one another.

408
00:32:46,720 --> 00:32:50,380
We need to focus on what are the needs of our spouse.

409
00:32:50,380 --> 00:32:54,840
And as we focus on the needs of our spouse, we'll become more and more unified.

410
00:32:54,840 --> 00:33:01,740
But in reality, in a good, healthy Christian relationship, what needs to happen is we need to focus our eyes on Jesus.

411
00:33:01,740 --> 00:33:06,080
And as we focus our eyes on Jesus, we'll get closer and closer together.

412
00:33:06,080 --> 00:33:10,820
And Barrett said, you know, I feel like this is just the perfect kind of illustration for this My Part Matters series.

413
00:33:10,860 --> 00:33:16,780
And I thought about it for a week or two, and I was like, man, it really is, except I think this is what the church looks like.

414
00:33:16,780 --> 00:33:17,440
Next slide.

415
00:33:17,440 --> 00:33:20,140
Maybe.

416
00:33:20,140 --> 00:33:21,020
There.

417
00:33:22,300 --> 00:33:23,500
Because here's what happens.

418
00:33:23,500 --> 00:33:31,620
Like, in marriage, like you're in this long-term relationship prior to your marriage where you're working really hard to get on the same level playing field.

419
00:33:31,620 --> 00:33:34,020
So you're starting from those bases of the triangles.

420
00:33:34,020 --> 00:33:39,780
But in the church, the church is supposed to be the most diverse organization ever.

421
00:33:39,780 --> 00:33:43,700
Like, we are filled with Jews, Greeks, slaves, free, male, female.

422
00:33:43,700 --> 00:33:46,200
Like, we are, like, as diverse as it comes.

423
00:33:46,200 --> 00:33:48,800
And so we're starting from all different directions.

424
00:33:49,320 --> 00:33:51,600
This looks like it could be a mess, right?

425
00:33:51,600 --> 00:33:57,840
Like, people that have all different backgrounds, all different political ideologies that come from different socioeconomic backgrounds.

426
00:33:57,840 --> 00:34:00,500
This looks like it should be and could be a mess.

427
00:34:00,500 --> 00:34:02,180
And sometimes it is.

428
00:34:02,180 --> 00:34:15,240
But if we put Jesus at the center, if we focus our eyes on him, we will slowly but surely over time come together.

429
00:34:15,520 --> 00:34:26,340
We will be knit together, fit together in our diversity, each understanding our own good things and becoming more and more like Jesus as individuals.

430
00:34:26,340 --> 00:34:30,160
We will become more and more like Jesus as a church.

431
00:34:30,160 --> 00:34:32,080
But here's what happens.

432
00:34:32,080 --> 00:34:32,520
You see there?

433
00:34:32,520 --> 00:34:36,100
There's a couple of arrows that are, like, banging into each other.

434
00:34:37,360 --> 00:34:43,640
Because what happens is sometimes we think we have our eyes on Jesus and when in reality we have our eyes on our own kind of desires.

435
00:34:43,640 --> 00:34:53,380
And what happens with a church that's modeled like this is because sometimes we'll get a little bit off track, we'll kind of drift, we'll end up running into somebody.

436
00:34:54,520 --> 00:35:06,840
And when we run into somebody, if our focus is Jesus, then we can refocus on Jesus.

437
00:35:06,840 --> 00:35:10,180
We can have meaningful conversations that are built on love and truth.

438
00:35:10,180 --> 00:35:16,100
We can say, hey, I don't understand how this thing that you're doing is actually making you become more like Jesus.

439
00:35:16,100 --> 00:35:17,580
You're making our church more like Jesus.

440
00:35:17,580 --> 00:35:19,480
You can have these meaningful conversations.

441
00:35:19,700 --> 00:35:21,700
I talked about this a little bit last week.

442
00:35:21,700 --> 00:35:27,140
I love the phrase, and I'll encourage our church to think this way moving forward.

443
00:35:27,140 --> 00:35:28,260
Believe the best.

444
00:35:28,260 --> 00:35:34,580
When you run into somebody and you think that you're headed towards Jesus and they think that they're headed towards Jesus,

445
00:35:34,580 --> 00:35:38,380
first and foremost, step back and believe the best about that, brother and sister and brother.

446
00:35:38,380 --> 00:35:43,260
Like, just assume that maybe it's possible that you're wrong and they're right.

447
00:35:43,260 --> 00:35:47,640
And then go to them in relationship and ask this question.

448
00:35:47,640 --> 00:35:48,460
Help me understand.

449
00:35:49,700 --> 00:35:55,380
Help me understand how this behavior, how this decision, how this thing that you're doing is you focusing on Jesus.

450
00:35:55,380 --> 00:36:03,640
And I think if we do that in truth and love, in relationship with one another,

451
00:36:03,640 --> 00:36:07,800
I think what will happen is oftentimes we'll get redirected.

452
00:36:07,800 --> 00:36:11,700
We'll think our eyes were on Jesus when in reality we were distracted.

453
00:36:11,700 --> 00:36:16,340
And based on that conversation, we'll realize that we need to recenter ourselves or focus ourselves.

454
00:36:17,360 --> 00:36:19,340
Or sometimes you're going to be right and they're going to be wrong.

455
00:36:19,340 --> 00:36:25,180
And out of grace and love, we both get our eyes refocused on Jesus together.

456
00:36:25,180 --> 00:36:37,040
Let's be a church that believes the best and that asks clarifying questions, that builds our maturity on this perfect balance of truth and love.

457
00:36:37,040 --> 00:36:42,700
So some final application questions before we transition to a time of communion.

458
00:36:42,700 --> 00:36:47,040
If you didn't grab communion, it might be awkward for you to stand up and go back now.

459
00:36:47,120 --> 00:36:49,700
But I don't think it's awkward, so I say just go do it.

460
00:36:49,700 --> 00:36:53,540
Here's a couple application questions.

461
00:36:53,540 --> 00:36:56,400
Which false teaching do you have the propensity to lean towards?

462
00:36:58,240 --> 00:37:02,760
Which of those two false teachings do you find yourself living in the most?

463
00:37:02,760 --> 00:37:06,700
Love without truth or truth without love?

464
00:37:06,700 --> 00:37:09,660
Is it possible?

465
00:37:09,660 --> 00:37:15,320
Is it possible that out of a reverence for God's word, you have become a person who cares more about truth,

466
00:37:15,320 --> 00:37:18,420
but doesn't have much love for your brothers and sisters in Christ?

467
00:37:20,500 --> 00:37:23,360
Sit with that, you and the Holy Spirit today, in this week.

468
00:37:23,360 --> 00:37:32,020
Or, is it possible that out of a deep love for all of God's image bearers,

469
00:37:32,020 --> 00:37:36,420
you have begun to redefine truth in your own image and the image of others,

470
00:37:36,420 --> 00:37:42,220
and you're unwilling to hold people accountable to the truth that God will ultimately one day hold them accountable for?

471
00:37:42,220 --> 00:37:44,800
Sit with that.

472
00:37:44,800 --> 00:37:47,560
Which one of these is your natural propensity?

473
00:37:47,560 --> 00:37:54,580
And the solution to this is to fix your eyes on Jesus, who perfectly balances truth and love.

474
00:37:54,580 --> 00:37:56,840
Let's be a people that daily fix our eyes on Jesus,

475
00:37:56,840 --> 00:38:00,920
who demonstrated the perfect balance of grace and truth

476
00:38:00,920 --> 00:38:05,100
by going to the cross to take on the punishment that you and I deserve.

477
00:38:05,100 --> 00:38:10,500
May we be a church that experiences an otherworldly type of unity,

478
00:38:10,500 --> 00:38:15,200
because as individuals, we've experienced the love and truth of Jesus,

479
00:38:15,200 --> 00:38:16,700
and we are becoming more like Him.

480
00:38:17,380 --> 00:38:17,700
Daily.

481
00:38:17,700 --> 00:38:22,380
We're going to finish our time together by taking communion.

482
00:38:22,380 --> 00:38:27,200
And we do this a lot around here, and we're going to continue to do it a lot.

483
00:38:27,200 --> 00:38:29,560
I don't know if it will be every week, but we're going to do it a lot.

484
00:38:29,560 --> 00:38:34,540
And the reason that we do it a lot is because no matter how bad my sermon is,

485
00:38:34,540 --> 00:38:36,840
and no matter how messed up the songs might get,

486
00:38:36,840 --> 00:38:38,580
like, this is why we're here.

487
00:38:40,780 --> 00:38:47,460
And this is the perfect visible representation of Jesus' truth and love.

488
00:38:48,520 --> 00:38:51,660
So if you're in here and you're a follower of Jesus, in a minute we're going to take communion.

489
00:38:51,660 --> 00:38:58,900
And what I want you to think about as you do that is that communion is this visible expression of truth and love that leads to unity.

490
00:38:58,900 --> 00:39:00,220
Truth.

491
00:39:00,700 --> 00:39:02,280
Your sin demands punishment.

492
00:39:02,280 --> 00:39:04,600
My sin demands punishment.

493
00:39:04,600 --> 00:39:08,020
We have offended a holy God.

494
00:39:10,360 --> 00:39:16,680
But love, God sent His one and only Son to take that punishment on our behalf.

495
00:39:16,680 --> 00:39:21,540
His body was broken and His blood was shed to pay the punishment for our sins,

496
00:39:21,540 --> 00:39:26,820
so that one day we'll all gather around a table,

497
00:39:26,820 --> 00:39:30,140
the wedding feast of the Lamb with Jesus at the head,

498
00:39:30,220 --> 00:39:32,900
and we will celebrate Him for all eternity,

499
00:39:32,900 --> 00:39:33,880
saying,

500
00:39:33,880 --> 00:39:37,880
Holy, Holy, Holy is the Lord God Almighty who was and is to come.

501
00:39:37,880 --> 00:39:42,940
Truth and love leads to unity when it's all centralized on Jesus.

502
00:39:42,940 --> 00:39:44,940
So if you're a believer, here in a second we'll take communion.

503
00:39:44,940 --> 00:39:47,400
If you're here and you're not really sure where you're at with Jesus,

504
00:39:47,400 --> 00:39:49,840
one, we're so glad that you're here.

505
00:39:49,840 --> 00:39:54,080
It's a great place to explore the teachings of Jesus,

506
00:39:54,080 --> 00:39:56,000
to consider the claims of Jesus.

507
00:39:57,180 --> 00:40:01,980
And the thing that we love the most about Jesus as believers is that He gets this right.

508
00:40:01,980 --> 00:40:06,480
And we think that it leads to an abundant life, a full and satisfied life,

509
00:40:06,480 --> 00:40:07,980
and we want you to experience that.

510
00:40:07,980 --> 00:40:11,020
So I'm going to ask you not to take communion,

511
00:40:11,020 --> 00:40:14,960
because this is for those of us that have submitted our lives to His Lordship.

512
00:40:14,960 --> 00:40:17,180
But what I will ask you to do is this week,

513
00:40:17,180 --> 00:40:18,780
go home and read the Gospel of John.

514
00:40:18,780 --> 00:40:21,180
And look for this balance.

515
00:40:21,180 --> 00:40:24,200
Look for Jesus being both loving and truthful.

516
00:40:24,780 --> 00:40:28,480
Holding people accountable to things that are ultimately going to lead to their destruction,

517
00:40:28,480 --> 00:40:31,440
but then providing a way for them to come back.

518
00:40:31,440 --> 00:40:36,000
And whoever you came with today, ask them.

519
00:40:36,000 --> 00:40:37,180
Talk to them.

520
00:40:37,180 --> 00:40:38,260
Have a conversation with them.

521
00:40:38,260 --> 00:40:40,620
If you came by yourself, if you just found this on the internet,

522
00:40:40,620 --> 00:40:42,460
or saw a new sign outside, or whatever,

523
00:40:42,460 --> 00:40:44,060
send us an email.

524
00:40:44,060 --> 00:40:47,580
I'd love to have a conversation with you about what this looks like.

525
00:40:47,680 --> 00:40:55,080
So, believers, let's take the body of Christ broken for us.

526
00:40:55,080 --> 00:41:03,260
We must drink the blood of Christ.

527
00:41:03,260 --> 00:41:04,320
It's in for us.

528
00:41:10,480 --> 00:41:15,820
Father, we thank you that you have had a perfect blueprint

529
00:41:15,820 --> 00:41:19,960
for healthy and vibrant expression of your community

530
00:41:19,960 --> 00:41:22,620
from the foundations of the earth.

531
00:41:22,620 --> 00:41:24,800
And you've given it to us through different Scriptures.

532
00:41:24,800 --> 00:41:28,180
And God, today I pray that we've seen that,

533
00:41:28,180 --> 00:41:32,620
that we understand that church unity is built on spiritual maturity,

534
00:41:32,700 --> 00:41:35,740
and that spiritual maturity is built on looking at Jesus

535
00:41:35,740 --> 00:41:38,240
and becoming more like Him day in and day out.

536
00:41:38,240 --> 00:41:40,580
And then doing that in community with one another.

537
00:41:40,580 --> 00:41:43,920
God, I pray that we would be a church that does that,

538
00:41:43,920 --> 00:41:47,760
that daily becomes more like you as individuals and as a community,

539
00:41:47,760 --> 00:41:55,000
so that the world can see the abundant life that you have for all of us

540
00:41:55,000 --> 00:41:56,580
who would just submit ourselves to you.

541
00:41:56,580 --> 00:41:58,960
God, I thank you for Jesus.

542
00:41:58,960 --> 00:42:00,140
It's his name, I pray.

543
00:42:00,140 --> 00:42:00,600
Amen.

544
00:42:00,600 --> 00:42:00,740
Amen.

545
00:42:02,360 --> 00:42:05,480
- I'm sorry.
